From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 08:57:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/36] No E369 in the arranger's automation view without a
 current clip

AutomationView::buttonAction() read the current clip's type and output type before anything else.
In the arranger's automation view right after a song load no clip has been entered, so there is
none: E369 (or a read through null) on any button. Read them only if there is a clip; the BACK +
horizontal encoder combination checks the arranger first, too.

v1.3.0 (#5243) already keeps SCALE, KIT, SYNTH, MIDI and CV away from the clip in the arranger's
automation view, which was the other half of the former 0013.

Test (beta-1.3/tests): arranger_automation_emu.py (fuzz seed 1071).
---
 src/deluge/gui/views/automation_view.cpp | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/deluge/gui/views/automation_view.cpp b/src/deluge/gui/views/automation_view.cpp
index a9c9d56c3..2034689f3 100644
--- a/src/deluge/gui/views/automation_view.cpp
+++ b/src/deluge/gui/views/automation_view.cpp
@@ -1142,8 +1142,9 @@ ActionResult AutomationView::buttonAction(hid::Button b, bool on, bool inCardRou
 
 	// Sean todo: need to refactor this to handle different automation view types more cleanly and safely
 
+	// The arranger's automation view may have no current clip at all (a song just loaded, no clip entered yet)
 	Clip* clip = getCurrentClip();
-	bool isAudioClip = clip->type == ClipType::AUDIO;
+	bool isAudioClip = clip != nullptr && clip->type == ClipType::AUDIO;
 
 	// these button actions are not used in the arranger or audio clip automation view
 	// (in arranger view the current clip is just whichever clip was last entered, so don't act on it)
@@ -1157,7 +1158,7 @@ ActionResult AutomationView::buttonAction(hid::Button b, bool on, bool inCardRou
 		}
 	}
 
-	OutputType outputType = clip->output->type;
+	OutputType outputType = clip != nullptr ? clip->output->type : OutputType::NONE;
 
 	// Scale mode button
 	if (b == SCALE_MODE) {
@@ -1550,7 +1551,7 @@ bool AutomationView::handleHorizontalEncoderButtonAction(bool on, bool isAudioCl
 bool AutomationView::handleBackAndHorizontalEncoderButtonComboAction(Clip* clip, bool on) {
 	// only allow clearing of a clip if you're on the automation overview
 	if (on && onAutomationOverview()) {
-		if (clip->type == ClipType::AUDIO || onArrangerView) {
+		if (onArrangerView || clip->type == ClipType::AUDIO) {
 			// clear all arranger automation
 			if (onArrangerView) {
 				Action* action = actionLogger.getNewAction(ActionType::ARRANGEMENT_CLEAR, ActionAddition::NOT_ALLOWED);
